# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Alslmany Crypto — environment
#
#  Every variable here is OPTIONAL. The site runs fully without any of them:
#  market data comes from public exchange endpoints that need no key.
#  Copy to .env.local and fill in only what you want.
#
#  All of these are read SERVER-SIDE ONLY and are never sent to the browser.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Telegram alerts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pushes an entry card when the bot opens a position and a result card when
# it closes one. Without a token the bot still trades; it just stays quiet.
#
#   1. In Telegram open @BotFather → /newbot → copy the token.
#   2. Open your new bot and press START once.
#   3. Set the token below. The chat id is detected from that first message.
#
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=123456789:AA...your_token...
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=            # optional — auto-detected when left empty


# ── 24/7 scanning ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Protects /api/cron/tick, which scans the market and manages open positions
# while nobody has the site open.
#
# Without this the endpoint stays CLOSED. It is never open by default — an
# unauthenticated endpoint that mutates a ledger is an invitation.
#
# Vercel Cron sends its own bearer token automatically. An external scheduler
# can instead call:  /api/cron/tick?key=<this value>
#
# Use a long random string:  openssl rand -hex 32
#
# CRON_SECRET=change_me_to_a_long_random_string


# ── Durable ledger ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Serverless instances are recycled, so without a durable store the bot's
# trade history resets whenever the platform restarts a container — and a
# track record that resets is not a track record.
#
# Any Upstash Redis database works; the free tier is enough. Create one at
# https://console.upstash.com and copy its REST credentials.
#
# When these are unset the ledger lives in process memory and the Bot desk
# says so on screen, so a reset is never mistaken for a change in strategy.
#
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://your-db.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=your_rest_token


# After editing, restart the dev server:  npm run dev
